Step 9: Resume, LinkedIn and applying (from month 8)

• Resume: one page only. Use a clean template, for example Jake's resume template on Overleaf
(overleaf.com). Order: education, skills, projects, internships, achievements. Every project line
should show what you built, the stack, and one result or number.
• LinkedIn: clear photo, headline like "MCA student | Python Backend Developer | FastAPI,
PostgreSQL", and post when you finish each project with a short demo video.
• Apply beyond campus: Internshala (internshala.com), Unstop (unstop.com), Naukri (naukri.com),
LinkedIn Jobs, Wellfound (wellfound.com) for startups, and Instahyre (instahyre.com).
• Internship: try hard to get one internship or a real freelance project during Phase 3. Even a small
paid or unpaid one with a startup changes how interviewers see you.
